**Headline result:** cache_coherency@32 is a clean A/B on the current build (FF5E7827): `dir_ex_tenure_floor=0` → **PASS 32/32**; floor=1 (default) → 0/32. The floor's mixed-era metadata composition is the single remaining blocker for this cell.

**Root-cause chain fully traced (was "silent EIO victims" for 2 sessions):** victims die in the rename phase when a lookup/shrink walks dir LEAF/FREE structure referencing a data block the in-core extent map lacks → `EFSCORRUPTED` → dirty `xfs_trans_cancel` → *"Corruption of in-memory data … Shutting down filesystem"* → per-mount EIO. The shutdown was never silent on the nodes — the artifact collector used `journalctl`, which rotates in ~85s under probe volume and dropped the XFS alerts (collection now uses `dmesg -T` first). Post-mortem `chk_mxfs` proves the platter is CONSISTENT at rest — the tear is a reader-side composition of an older map with newer structure, cornered to cold-iget of an evicted dir inode adopting the legitimately-lagging home image.

**Real bugs found and fixed (kept — verified non-regressive by the 32/32 run):** (1) every bmbt leaf write bypassed the sess66 tenure-authority gate via the sess63 FUA passthrough — stale unlogged leaf re-publishes were landing freely; the gate now runs on the FUA path, plus a read-side tenure stamp so fresh-read images stay re-publishable (the bare gate alone starved the platter). (2) A never-adopt-older changecount guard in the reload. (3) run.sh: exclusive flock (rival-run protection), dmesg-first log collection, and the P-HOLE-DISK probe ungated from `ino<=256`.

**Infrastructure sabotage eliminated:** both predecessor ccloop sessions were still ALIVE post-relay and actively launching rival runs that power-cycled nodes mid-test (the "membership splits" and one whole 0/32 were fabricated). Killed, documented in memory, and guarded by the run lock.

**Ready for next session:** build 9C813539 (v0.10.8) is compiled with the decisive discriminator — `iget_age_ms` on the P14 hole probe — which will confirm or refute the cold-iget mechanism in one run, plus complete write-history instrumentation. The handoff memories (`AAA-ccloop46ef-sess3-STATE-…` and `…-END-build-9C813539-next-steps`) carry the full evidence chain and the exact next sequence through to the 1/2/4/8/16/32 ladder.

